---
import LightsaberExclamation from "@components/ui/LightsaberExclamation.astro";
import Layout from "src/layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<style>
  .wrapper {
    box-sizing: border-box;
    height: 100%;
    width: fit-content;
    max-width: min(1000px, 90dvw);
    min-height: 100dvh;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 2em;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 4em;
  }

  .tagline {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-rows: 1fr 1fr;
    margin-bottom: 1em;
  }

  .tagline span.right-aligned {
    text-align: right;
  }

  section {
    position: relative;
  }

  section::before {
    position: absolute;
    content: "";
    top: -1em;
    left: -1em;
    width: calc(100% + 2em);
    height: calc(100% + 2em);
    opacity: 0.8;
    background-color: var(--background-color);
    border-radius: 0.25em;
    z-index: -1;
  }

  section p {
    font-size: 0.9em;
    text-align: justify;
  }

  .title {
    position: relative;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 1.25em;
    margin-bottom: 1em;
  }

  .title::before {
    position: absolute;
    content: "";
    background-color: var(--text-color);
    bottom: -0.25em;
    left: 0;
    width: 100%;
    height: 1px;
    z-index: -1;
    opacity: 0.5;
  }

  .grayscale {
    filter: grayscale(50%);
  }

  @media screen and (max-width: 480px) {
    .wrapper {
      padding: 2em;
      max-width: 100dvw;
    }

    .section::before {
      opacity: 1;
    }

    .tagline {
      font-size: 2.2em;
    }
  }
</style>
<Layout title="About Me" description="Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet">
  <main class="wrapper">
    <h1 class="tagline">
      <span>Hello there!</span>
      <span class="right-aligned">General Kenobi<LightsaberExclamation /></span>
    </h1>

    <section>
      <h2 class="title">TL;DR</h2>
      <p>
        Hi, I'm Aleksandar, originally from North Macedonia, living in northern
        Italy since I was young.
      </p>
      <p>
        I enjoy tinkering with tech, mainly for the web: building fast, reliable
        applications, crafting visuals, and creating immersive 3D experiences.
      </p>
      <p>
        Evenings are usually football, friends and family, and a stack of other
        hobbies.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="title">Expanded intro</h2>
      <p>
        I stepped into tech back in 2017, building server-rendered
        <code>Node + Pug</code> sites. Soon after I went deep into
        <code>React</code>, shipping a steady stream of data-heavy SaaS and
        marketplace dashboards.
      </p>
      <p>
        Along the way I picked up graphics work, raw <code>WebGL</code>,
        <code>WebGPU</code>, and the maths that makes 3D tick, both with and
        without <code>Three.js</code>, and more recently inside
        <code>Godot</code> as well.
      </p>
      <p>The open-ended nature of graphics keeps me learning every day.</p>
      <p>
        I like to join projects early: sketching an MVP, spotting pitfalls, and
        agreeing on trade-offs with designers, back-end devs, QA, and everyone
        else in the loop. Lining up the basics first makes the initial build
        smoother and lets us iterate on real user feedback instead of re-doing
        avoidable mistakes.
      </p>
      <p>
        A few edge cases still slip through, but each one becomes a lesson for
        next time.
      </p>
      <p>
        Below you'll find a concise career timeline, a snapshot of my toolkit,
        and a quick way to reach me if you'd like the full résumé.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="title">Professional journey</h2>
      <p>
        Here my career path... Lorem, ipsum dolor sit amet consectetur
        adipisicing elit. Similique architecto repellendus consequatur
        voluptatibus dolore fugiat esse voluptatum, optio praesentium eum ex
        placeat nemo nesciunt dolorum ipsum sapiente, quisquam dolorem dicta.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>
